course: dictionary
lesson: 12542
title: Deteriorate: getting worse
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To deteriorate means to become worse, little by little or quickly, as time goes on. «The weather deteriorated during the afternoon, and the sunny picnic turned into a soggy mess.» The sky went from blue to grey and the rain began, so deteriorated means got worse.
explain: Things can deteriorate too. «The old wooden bridge began to deteriorate after years of rain.» Wood can rot and break down, so the bridge gets weaker. Food, metal and paper can deteriorate in the same way.
explain: The opposite of deteriorate is improve. If the weather deteriorated, it got worse; if it improved, it got better. Look for clues such as «over time» or «more and more» to spot this word in a text.
fact: To deteriorate means to become worse over time.
fact: Deteriorate is a verb, so it changes: deteriorates, deteriorated, deteriorating.
fact: «Deteriorating» describes a situation that is getting worse, as in «a deteriorating situation».
fact: «Deteriorate rapidly» means to get worse very quickly.
fact: The opposite of deteriorate is improve.
exercise: «The weather deteriorated during the afternoon.» What does deteriorated mean? | *Became worse | Became brighter and warmer | Stopped completely | Stayed exactly the same
exercise: «The old wooden bridge began to deteriorate after years of rain.» What is the opposite of deteriorate? | Repeat | *Improve | Rot | Collapse
exercise: Nadia says, «The fish began to deteriorate on the hot sand.» What does she mean? | The fish began to smell of roses | The fish began to grow bigger | *The fish began to go off and spoil | The fish began to swim away
test: «Her health deteriorated over the winter.» Which word means the opposite of deteriorated? | *improved | broke | rotted | worsened
test: Maya says, «Deteriorate means to get better.» Is she right? | Yes, it means to get better | Yes, it means to stay the same | *No, it means to become worse | No, it means to be very loud
exam: «The situation deteriorated rapidly after the storm.» What does deteriorated mean here? | Was cleaned up | Got better quickly | *Got worse quickly | Stayed the same
